# {{ name }}

> A short description of this service...

A Nest app, bundled by rspack into `dist/main.js` through `labuild`. Its business logic lives in
[`@example/{{ name }}-domain`](../../packages/{{ name }}-domain).

## Modes

`SERVER_MODE` picks what this process serves. Every mode also serves `GET /status` on `PORT`.

{{#if usesGraphQL}}
- `GRAPHQL`: a federated GraphQL subgraph at `/graphql`. In development its schema is written to
  [`@example/{{ name }}-graphql-schema`](../../packages/{{ name }}-graphql-schema), which the gateway reads.
{{/if}}
{{#if usesGrpc}}
- `GRPC`: the `{{ pascalCase name }}Service` from [`@example/{{ name }}-proto`](../../packages/{{ name }}-proto) on
  `GRPC_PORT`.
{{/if}}

`pnpm start` at the repo root runs each mode as its own process, with ports from
[`@example/sears-catalog`](../../packages/sears-catalog/src/deploymentCatalog.ts).

## Scripts

| Script | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `pnpm dev` | Bundles in watch mode and restarts on every change, including changes to workspace packages, which it compiles from source. Reads `.env.development`. |
| `pnpm build` | Production bundle. Compiled workspace packages come from their `dist` (turbo builds them first). |
| `pnpm start` | Runs the production bundle with plain `node`. |
| `pnpm test` | vitest, from source. Needs no build. |
| `pnpm docker:build` | Builds the image from the repo root with `turbo prune`. |

## Imports

The app imports its own modules through its `imports` map (`#app.module`, `#graphql/graphql.module`), which
points at `src`. rspack resolves those at build time, so the bundle runs without them.
